        <p>WARRINGTON CORPORATION BILL. The time allowed for lodging petitions against this Bill expired at 3 p.m. on Tuesday. One peti- tion against the Bill, on behalf of the Middleton Hall Estate, was deposited,but terms were arranged and the petition withdrawn. The Bill, therefore, may be considered to be passed subject to any amendments made by the promoters. The Bill was read a second time in the House of Lords on Tues- day evening.</p>
